  {"date": "2025-06-28", "venue": "Moody Center", "city": "Austin", "state": "TX", "gap": 8, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Kicking off what has seemingly become a trend in 2025 of extended \"2001\" style intros, what we get here is the first truly significant departure from rote play since 8/16/97. A noticeably slower tempo in the \"Landlady\" section still slightly mars these modern outings but the relatively clean performance and extra love shown to the intro demand our attention.", "out": ">", "next": "Free", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-15", "venue": "TD Pavilion at the Mann", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 7, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Follows in the footsteps of 6/28/25 with an intro that further pushes the bounds of \"PYITE\" consisting of skronky guitar and lots of synth bass which is later intensified by Trey soloing and then drops directly back into the song. Tremendous opener.", "out": ">", "next": "Everything's Right", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-23", "venue": "Forest Hills Stadium", "city": "Forest Hills", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Serving as the Set 2 opener for the first time since NYE '19, this \"PYITE\" gets an extra flourish from Trey and Page in its opening. Strong play continues throughout, before > into \"Ghost\".", "out": ">", "next": "Ghost", "xprev": "The Squirming Coil", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-09-14", "venue": "Coca-Cola Amphitheater", "city": "Birmingham", "state": "AL", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "next": "Mike's Song", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-12-28", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The final version of \"PYITE's\" remarkable 2025 once again features an extended improvisational intro. Syncopated funk, synths, and effects all feature prominently in this newfound addition to the song's structure.", "out": ">", "prev": "Wolfman's Brother", "in": ">", "next": "Sigma Oasis", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2026-04-30", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 13, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "2026 picks up where \u201825 left off in regards to the extended intro section of this classic rocker. The band remains committed to \u2018punching up\u2019 the play here with synth effects as well as some additional clean leads from Trey to guide the affair into the song proper. The \u201cLandlady\u201d section still sadly suffers from some minor pacing and performance issues.", "prev": "Dirt", "next": "Golgi Apparatus", "nb": 1},
